1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,682
Imagine you are standing at a hospital billing counter at nine o'clock at night.

2
00:00:04,682 --> 00:00:13,347
The bill is four and a half lakh rupees, and your cashless claim, where the insurance company pays the hospital directly, has just been denied.

3
00:00:13,347 --> 00:00:15,686
We told this story in our last video.

4
00:00:15,686 --> 00:00:17,617
Here is what you need to know from it.

5
00:00:17,617 --> 00:00:20,735
A cashless denial is not the end of your claim.

6
00:00:20,735 --> 00:00:24,057
You can pay the hospital, and claim the money back later.

7
00:00:24,057 --> 00:00:27,728
And if the company still says no, there is a four-step plan.

8
00:00:27,728 --> 00:00:29,063
Collect your papers.

9
00:00:29,063 --> 00:00:32,311
File for reimbursement and write to the grievance officer.

10
00:00:32,311 --> 00:00:34,421
Register on Bima Bharosa.

11
00:00:34,421 --> 00:00:37,298
And step four, the Insurance Ombudsman.

12
00:00:37,298 --> 00:00:43,732
So you paid the bill from your pocket, collected your hospital papers, came home, and filed for reimbursement.

13
00:00:43,732 --> 00:00:46,921
Three weeks later, an email lands in your inbox.

14
00:00:46,921 --> 00:01:00,096
Either the insurance company rejects your claim all over again... or worse, out of your four and a half lakh rupee bill, they approve just one lakh twenty thousand, and cut the remaining three lakh thirty thousand rupees.

15
00:01:00,096 --> 00:01:04,485
At that moment, many families think they only have two choices.

16
00:01:04,485 --> 00:01:05,519
Choice one.

17
00:01:05,519 --> 00:01:11,115
Hire a lawyer, go to consumer court, and wait, often for a long time, for a verdict.

18
00:01:11,115 --> 00:01:12,694
Or choice two.

19
00:01:12,694 --> 00:01:23,173
Answer one of those ads for a private claim recovery service, which promises to fight your case, but some ask for twenty percent or more of the money they recover as their fee.

20
00:01:23,173 --> 00:01:24,468
Stop right there.

21
00:01:24,468 --> 00:01:27,900
Before you pick either door, there is a third one.

22
00:01:27,900 --> 00:01:29,725
Step four of that plan.

23
00:01:29,725 --> 00:01:33,862
Today, we open that door fully, from start to finish.

24
00:01:33,862 --> 00:01:36,624
Filing a complaint costs zero rupees.

25
00:01:36,624 --> 00:01:40,923
If the Ombudsman passes an award, it is binding on the insurance company.

26
00:01:40,923 --> 00:01:49,232
And if the company does not challenge the award, but pays it late, it has to pay you a penalty of five thousand rupees for every day of delay.

27
00:01:49,232 --> 00:01:51,562
Welcome to Be Practical with Kishore.

28
00:01:51,562 --> 00:02:04,157
Today, I will show you one common mistake that gets complaints turned away at the door, how to file on the official website step by step, what happens at the hearing, and what the company must do after it loses.

29
00:02:04,157 --> 00:02:07,358
All without paying a single rupee to middlemen.

30
00:02:07,358 --> 00:02:10,847
Let's break it down... in plain, simple English.

